## FILE 2: src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/NoranProtocolDecoder.java

### CHANGE: Validate GPS coordinates before using (prevent "longitude out of range" error)

**Location:** decodeLastPacket() method (around line 103)

**Find:**
```java
if (buf.readableBytes() >= 57) {
    newFormat = true;
    Position position = new Position(getProtocolName());
    double lon = buffer.readFloat();
    double lat = buffer.readFloat();
    position.setLongitude(lon);
    position.setLatitude(lat);
    // ... rest of code ...
}
```

**Replace with:**
```java
if (buf.readableBytes() >= 57) {
    newFormat = true;
    Position position = new Position(getProtocolName());
    
    // ✅ READ COORDINATES FIRST
    float lonRaw = buffer.readFloat();
    float latRaw = buffer.readFloat();
    
    // ✅ VALIDATE: Skip position creation if coordinates are invalid (ACK-only packet)
    if (Math.abs(lonRaw) > 180.0 || Math.abs(latRaw) > 90.0) {
        return null; // This is an ACK packet without valid GPS data
    }
    
    position.setLongitude(lonRaw);
    position.setLatitude(latRaw);
    // ... rest of code ...
}
```

